    "turn_text": "Well, you know, I grew up in the 60s, and like so many others, I sat and listened every evening as Walter Cronkite gave the play-by-play on the war and what was happening. I lost a first cousin in 1968. He was in the Army. and was killed in Vietnam. So I had a strong sense of service to country and so it was not a surprise to me that I wanted to do this. Now I will tell you that when I joined they told many of us that it was likely that we would be going direct duty assignment to Vietnam right out of basic training. But it was in our 17th day of training that the Paris Peace Accords were signed and so all of a sudden the whole plan ahead changed and we all were reclassified and we had to choose our perspective career areas and I just got really, really",
