    "turn_text": "I had signed up under what was called a guaranteed career area, guaranteed field, which was electronics. I had scored high on the electronics part of the ASVAB. And so I knew that I was probably going to be an electronics technician of some sort. Little did I know that my best friend in high school, his father, was the superintendent over the training devices section where we taught student pilots how to fly on simulators. And to this day, he's deceased now. My friend's father is deceased, so I never got a chance to ask him whether or not he called and put in a good word or did anything like that. But I was extremely pleased when I was selected for the career field to be a flight simulator instructor and maintenance technician on the simulators. That was about as close to flying that I thought I would actually get myself.",
