    "turn_text": "I had never been to, I did do one semester of college at Mississippi State University after graduating from high school. My stepfather had gotten stationed in Columbus, Mississippi, so I went one semester there. But I never lived on campus, never really experienced the college life. When I was accepted for the scholarship, they sent me to Troy University in Alabama. It was called Troy State at the time, and we lived right there on campus. I was married with two children at the time. And the comradery, I became the commander or the cadet commander of the ROTC detachment, had a great 18 months there and couldn't have asked for a better experience to get started off on a commission",
