    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91985.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 50,
    "turn_text": "Well, I moved very quickly into management after I finished graduate school in 84. I became a section chief. and then later went to Air Command and Staff College. Developed was a program manager on some large systems implementations. It wasn't until I got to Eglin Air Force Base in 92 that, I'm sorry, 93 that the learning curve really took off because I had been a software engineer never worked tactically at the base level and all of a sudden I was a squadron commander over the Air Force's largest communications squadron at the time, the equivalent of a small city with five active air wings. three airports and all the runways and the navigation systems to maintain and a tactical unit that I was responsible for that deployed in support of a fighter wing. So there was a big learning curve there.",
