  {
    "episode_id": 91985,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91985.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 67,
    "turn_text": "Comradery that can't be found really. You can't find it anywhere else. Congressman, we've just got a few minutes left in our conversation here. We talked about the terrorist threat that was emerging in the 1990s, obviously, since then. We had the coal 9-11, obviously, and it's been the focal point of our foreign policy ever since. Right now, of course, one of the major threats is the Islamic State, and there's a lot of debate right now about what the proper policy is. I don't want to get too political, but from the leadership that you gain from over a quarter century in the military, what type of general approaches needed when a threat like this presents",
