    "turn_text": "doing? It is a never-ending battle. And anyone who doesn't understand that it's going to require increased and constant vigilance in order to stay ahead of the problem, it's the nature of computing and communicating technologies. Computers can do only two things. they can add strings of ones and zeros together, and they can shift strings of ones and zeros one direction or another to the left or to the right. It's an on off switch. And as long as computers function off of ones and zeros at the core, you're going to have bad guys that are going to find a way to get into them. Because programming, developing computer code with ones and zeros is not that tough. I've done it. So it is a problem that we have to stay out in front of because communicating and computing technology basically controls the world today. You're talking to me right now while you're managing this on an iPhone. All of our financial systems, our healthcare systems, our power and energy systems, not to mention almost all of our military infrastructure, radar. the capability to laser direct a weapon system. That's all communicating technology, backed and undergirded by a strong platform of computing technology. And we're going to have to stay on top of it because if the bad guys get in, it's going to be",
